From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:45:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] denormal_disabler: Don't use inline assembly with MSVC

The ARM implementation uses GCC style inline assembly, which MSVC does not
support (upstream only builds for Windows on ARM with clang-cl). Leave the
disabler as a no-op there, like the x86 code already is for compilers other
than clang.
---
diff --git a/webrtc/rtc_base/denormal_disabler.cc b/webrtc/rtc_base/denormal_disabler.cc
--- a/webrtc/rtc_base/denormal_disabler.cc
+++ b/webrtc/rtc_base/denormal_disabler.cc
@@ -20,8 +20,11 @@
 #define WEBRTC_DENORMAL_DISABLER_X86_SUPPORTED
 #endif
 
+// The ARM implementation uses GCC style inline assembly, which MSVC does not
+// support.
 #if defined(WEBRTC_DENORMAL_DISABLER_X86_SUPPORTED) || \
-    defined(WEBRTC_ARCH_ARM_FAMILY)
+    (defined(WEBRTC_ARCH_ARM_FAMILY) &&                \
+     (defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)))
 #define WEBRTC_DENORMAL_DISABLER_SUPPORTED
 #endif
 
-- 
2.49.0

